    "teach_8": {
      "id": "teach_8",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Capstone: separate three questions in your head.\n\n1. What fraction of the tank must change?\n2. What is the active rate?\n3. Is that rate filling or emptying?\n\nOnly then calculate the time.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_8_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_8_step": {
      "id": "teach_8_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Example: a tank is 1/3 full. A pipe fills at 1/9 tank per hour.\nMissing = 2/3.\nTime = 2/3 ÷ 1/9 = 6 hours.\n\nThat same three-step habit will survive much harder pipe questions.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_8"
        }
      ]
    },
